      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This has been happening to me for a while too. I've heard of it happening in other games too. \n\nI suspect the problem is that VRChat closes, but the EAC process keeps running (since you can't delete one of the EAC files because it's \"opened in another program\")\n\nIt fixed itself after waiting for a very long time (upwards of- or longer than an hour of VRChat still showing as running) or like OP said, when restarting the PC and thus exiting all running processes. \n\nQuitting steam also shows the game as not running anymore, but this just gives an EAC error when you try to launch the game, because an EAC process is still invisibly running in the background somewhere. It doesn't show up on task manager.\n\nSeeing as this happened in other games too, I'm not sure if VRC can do much about it, but I hope I'm wrong on that because it's a very annoying problem to deal with.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
